(SCJC had but three constitutional remedies from which to choose. But the SCJC did not) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 678 Tm
102 Tz
(“issue an order of public censure or . . . recommend to a review tribunal the removal or) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 648.25 Tm
100 Tz
(retirement” of Judge Keller, because a public warning is not a censure. A public warning) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 618.25 Tm
98 Tz
(is a sanction:) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.5 588.25 Tm
100 Tz
(“Sanction” means an order issued by the commission under Section 1-a\(8\),) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 573.399 Tm
(Article V, Texas Constitution, providing for a private or public admonition,) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.25 558.7 Tm
102 Tz
(warning, or reprimand or requiring that a person obtain additional training) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.25 543.6 Tm
97 Tz
(or education.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 522.7 Tm
103 Tz
(Tex. Gov) Tj
1 0 0 1 123.6 522.5 Tm
106 Tz
(’t Code § 33.001\(10\) \(App. H\). A censure is a different punishment from a) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 492.75 Tm
98 Tz
(sanction such as a public warning:) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.5 462.75 Tm
100 Tz
(“Censure” means an order of denunciation issued by the commission under) Tj
1 0 0 1 108.5 447.849 Tm
109 Tz
(Section 1-a\(8\), Article V, Texas Constitution, or an order issued by a) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 433 Tm
99 Tz
(review tribunal under Section 1-a\(9\), Article V, Texas Constitution.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 412.049 Tm
102 Tz
(Tex. Gov) Tj
