99 Tz
(The Oral Execution-day Procedures Were Not a Law, Canon, or Rule) Tj
1 0 0 1 144.25 573.149 Tm
98 Tz
(Imposing a Sanctionable Duty on Judge Keller. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 546.5 Tm
112 Tz
/OPBaseFont0 13 Tf
(As the SCJC admits in its Charging Document, the CCA’s execution-day) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 516.5 Tm
101 Tz
(procedures were an unwritten “oral protocol” as of September 25, 2007. The SCJC does) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 486.75 Tm
106 Tz
(not contend that this “oral protocol” was a law, canon of conduct, or court rule. The) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 456.75 Tm
103 Tz
(SCJC alleges that the oral protocol was a “duty of Judge Keller’s office,” but offers no) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 426.949 Tm
109 Tz
(citation to support the allegation – because no legal authority exists to support the) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.5 397 Tm
103 Tz
(allegation. Fortunately for the citizens of Texas, the Commission does not promulgate) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 367 Tm
(laws or create “duties of office” that are binding on elected officials like Judge Keller.) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 337.199 Tm
100 Tz
(The actual rules and laws governing Judge Keller and the CCA are codified in article 5 of) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 307.199 Tm
101 Tz
(the Texas Constitution, chapter 22 of the Texas Government Code, and the Texas Rules) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 277.449 Tm
102 Tz
(of Appellate Procedure – none of which, it should go without saying, mention the “oral) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 247.449 Tm
101 Tz
(protocol” at the heart of the SCJC’s latest allegations against Judge Keller. She might as) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 217.699 Tm
99 Tz
(well be accused of violating the “Don’t Mess With Texas” motto \(although at least that is) Tj
1 0 0 1 72.25 187.899 Tm
100 Tz
(written\). The “oral protocol” simply was not a duty of office.) Tj
1 0 0 1 108 157.699 Tm
101 Tz
(As pleaded by the SCJC, the “oral protocol” provided that “[a]ll communications) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 127.949 Tm
113 Tz
(regarding the scheduled execution shall first be referred to the assigned judge.”) Tj
1 0 0 1 72 97.949 Tm
99 Tz
(Notwithstanding the fact that Judge Keller did not receive any communication of any sort) Tj
